<title>GERMANY: German crops boosted by recent rains.</title>
<headline>German crops boosted by recent rains.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH, Germany 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rains over the past six days have helped German crops recover from an earlier dry spell, the national meteorological office DWD said.</p>
<p>&quot;I have no worries for the crops. It will stay rainy in May and temperatures will improve,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>He added crops had a good chance of recovering from minimal damage suffered in spring wheat and beet regions because of cold weather this month.</p>
<p>Day temperatures around 15 to 20 degrees were forecast for the next seven days, when maize plantings should be completed.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
